{
  "$comment": [
    "The benchmark's own reference data about the world: which programs are in scope,",
    "what they are called, and which internet domains they operate. This is the answer",
    "key, so it is authored and frozen here and is NEVER regenerated from the knowledge",
    "base under test. A scoring input derived from the system being measured cannot",
    "attribute a score change to that system: if the corpus can move the key, a corpus",
    "edit can raise the score without improving an answer.",
    "",
    "`domains` are registrable domains the operator itself publishes on. They are",
    "deliberately domains rather than exact page URLs, because 'this is the operator's",
    "own site' is a fact about the program, while 'this exact URL is in our corpus' is a",
    "fact about the corpus. Exact-URL matching credited a citation only when the corpus",
    "already held that page, which is circular for a corpus-backed condition and unfair",
    "to an agent that finds the operator's own pages the corpus never captured.",
    "",
    "Authored 2026-09-15. Editing this file changes what the benchmark recognises, so",
    "treat a change here like a change to a rubric: scores either side of it are not",
    "directly comparable."
  ],
